<title>USA: IMF puts country data on Internet.</title>
<headline>IMF puts country data on Internet.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Monetary Fund said it was making available statistical data for six countries via its Internet site starting on Friday.</p>
<p>The six countries were Canada, Mexico, Singapore, South Africa, Switzerland and Hong Kong, the IMF said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Links to the data would be available at http://dsbb@imf.org, the IMF said.</p>
<p>Links to data sites for Finland, Israel, Japan and Turkey are expected shorty, it said.</p>
</text>
